{"title":"Career Roadmap · UX Research Assistant","role":"UX Research Assistant","summary":"A UX Research Assistant (UXRA) supports research that helps organisations understand how people think, behave, perceive, and interact with products or services.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Neuroscience / Cognitive Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"A UX Research Assistant (UXRA) supports research that helps organisations understand how people think, behave, perceive, and interact with products or services."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc in Neuroscience / Cognitive Science, this is a strong interdisciplinary career pathway. Neuroscience and cognitive science provide useful foundations in perception, attention, memory, decision-making, behaviour, experimentation, and human cognition. However, the student must add practical UX research, qualitative research, usability testing, product thinking, and research communication skills."},{"type":"p","text":"The most realistic entry titles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX Research Assistant"},{"text":"UX Research Intern"},{"text":"User Research Assistant"},{"text":"Junior UX Researcher"},{"text":"Research Assistant – User Experience"},{"text":"Human Factors Research Assistant"},{"text":"Customer/User Insights Analyst"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Cognitive Science","Research Methods","UX","Data Analysis"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Entry & Foundation"},{"text":"Research methods, UX fundamentals, usability testing, qualitative/quantitative analysis"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"UX Researcher"},{"text":"Independent studies, product research, behavioural analysis"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior UX / Research Specialist"},{"text":"Complex research, strategy, experimentation, human factors"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Research Leadership"},{"text":"Behavioural science, AI-human interaction, research strategy"}]]}]},{"heading":"What Does a UX Research Assistant Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A UX Research Assistant supports researchers in understanding users, their needs, behaviours, frustrations, motivations, and decision-making patterns."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Recruit research participants"},{"text":"Prepare interview guides"},{"text":"Conduct user interviews"},{"text":"Assist with usability testing"},{"text":"Observe user behaviour"},{"text":"Prepare surveys"},{"text":"Analyse research data"},{"text":"Transcribe interviews"},{"text":"Code qualitative responses"},{"text":"Create research summaries"},{"text":"Build user personas"},{"text":"Analyse user journeys"},{"text":"Support research presentations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Typical research workflow"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Question"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Plan"},{"type":"h","text":"Participant Recruitment"},{"type":"h","text":"Interviews / Surveys / Usability Tests"},{"type":"h","text":"Data Collection"},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative + Quantitative Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Insights"},{"type":"h","text":"Product Recommendations"}]},{"heading":"Why Neuroscience / Cognitive Science Fits","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This degree can provide useful knowledge in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Perception"},{"type":"p","text":"Understanding how users perceive:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Visual information"},{"text":"Sound"},{"text":"Colours"},{"text":"Layouts"},{"text":"Interfaces"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Attention"},{"type":"p","text":"Understanding:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Distraction"},{"text":"Cognitive load"},{"text":"Selective attention"},{"text":"Information overload"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Memory"},{"type":"p","text":"Understanding:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Recognition vs recall"},{"text":"Working memory"},{"text":"Learning"},{"text":"Information retention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Decision-making"},{"type":"p","text":"Understanding:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Choice behaviour"},{"text":"Risk perception"},{"text":"Biases"},{"text":"Cognitive shortcuts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Human behaviour"},{"type":"p","text":"Understanding:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Emotion"},{"text":"Behavioural patterns"},{"text":"User expectations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The important step is converting this theoretical knowledge into applied UX research methodology."}]},{"heading":"Build Skills During B.Sc","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Cognitive Science & Research Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong foundations in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Neuroscience"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain anatomy"},{"text":"Neural systems"},{"text":"Sensory processing"},{"text":"Cognitive neuroscience"},{"text":"Behavioural neuroscience"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cognitive science"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Perception"},{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Learning"},{"text":"Language"},{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"Problem-solving"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Social psychology"},{"text":"Developmental psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"Basic regression"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Research Methods"},{"type":"p","text":"This is a critical year."},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Statistical testing"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"ANOVA"},{"text":"Effect sizes"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Thematic analysis"},{"text":"Coding"},{"text":"Affinity mapping"},{"text":"Content analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research ethics"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Informed consent"},{"text":"Participant privacy"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Data protection"},{"text":"Research ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to produce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research protocols"},{"text":"Interview guides"},{"text":"Survey instruments"},{"text":"Research reports"},{"text":"Executive summaries"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — UX Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Now connect cognitive science to product research."},{"type":"h","text":"UX fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User experience"},{"text":"User-centred design"},{"text":"Human-computer interaction"},{"text":"Information architecture"},{"text":"User journeys"},{"text":"Interaction design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Usability research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to conduct:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Moderated usability testing"},{"text":"Unmoderated testing"},{"text":"Task-based testing"},{"text":"Think-aloud studies"},{"text":"Heuristic evaluation"},{"text":"Comparative testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"User interviews"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview planning"},{"text":"Open-ended questioning"},{"text":"Probing"},{"text":"Neutral questioning"},{"text":"Avoiding leading questions"},{"text":"Interview note-taking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Survey research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Questionnaire design"},{"text":"Response scales"},{"text":"Question wording"},{"text":"Survey bias"},{"text":"Sampling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Professional UX Research"},{"type":"p","text":"If the programme includes a fourth year, develop advanced research capabilities."},{"type":"h","text":"Mixed-method research"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative + Quantitative"},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["User interviews","Identify themes","Survey 500 users","Validate patterns","Product recommendation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Behavioural analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Funnel analysis"},{"text":"Retention"},{"text":"Conversion"},{"text":"User flows"},{"text":"Cohort analysis"},{"text":"A/B testing fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Product analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn basic:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Python/R"},{"text":"Product analytics tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research communication"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to convert research findings into:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Evidence","Insight","Recommendation","Product Decision"]}]},{"heading":"Four-Year Development Plan","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Main Focus","Practical Output"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Cognitive science, psychology, statistics"},{"text":"Behavioural research project"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Interview + survey study"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"UX research & usability"},{"text":"Usability testing project"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Mixed methods & product analytics"},{"text":"Complete UX research case study"}]]}]},{"heading":"Practical Project Roadmap","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Usability Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose an existing website or mobile application."},{"type":"p","text":"Define:"},{"type":"note","label":"Research question","text":"\"What prevents new users from completing the task efficiently?\""},{"type":"p","text":"Recruit participants and observe them performing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Registration"},{"text":"Search"},{"text":"Checkout"},{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"Content discovery"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Measure:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Task completion"},{"text":"Time on task"},{"text":"Errors"},{"text":"User satisfaction"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Produce a research report."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — User Interview Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Interview a small, ethically recruited group of users about a product category."},{"type":"p","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Goals"},{"text":"Pain points"},{"text":"Behaviours"},{"text":"Expectations"},{"text":"Frustrations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Perform:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Interview","Transcription","Coding","Themes","Insights"]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Cognitive Load Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a small controlled study comparing two interface designs."},{"type":"p","text":"Measure:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Task completion time"},{"text":"Error rate"},{"text":"Recall"},{"text":"Subjective workload"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Connect the findings to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Working memory"},{"text":"Cognitive load"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is particularly valuable for a neuroscience/cognitive-science student."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Survey-Based UX Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct a user survey measuring:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Satisfaction"},{"text":"Usability"},{"text":"Feature preferences"},{"text":"User expectations"},{"text":"Frustrations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse using:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"R/Python"},{"text":"Power BI"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Accessibility Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Study how users with different accessibility needs interact with a digital interface."},{"type":"p","text":"Investigate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Text readability"},{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"Contrast"},{"text":"Keyboard interaction"},{"text":"Screen-reader compatibility"},{"text":"Cognitive accessibility"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Produce evidence-based recommendations."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 6 — A/B Testing Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Use a simulated or appropriate public dataset."},{"type":"p","text":"Compare:"},{"type":"h","text":"Version A vs Version B"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conversion rate"},{"text":"Completion rate"},{"text":"Engagement"},{"text":"Statistical significance"},{"text":"Effect size"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Explain whether the observed difference is practically meaningful, not just statistically significant."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"h","text":"Technology companies"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX Research Intern"},{"text":"User Research Intern"},{"text":"Product Research Intern"},{"text":"Human Factors Intern"},{"text":"Design Research Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Startups"},{"type":"p","text":"Startups can provide broad exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"Product testing"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Customer discovery"},{"text":"Product analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research organisations"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive science laboratories"},{"text":"Human-computer interaction labs"},{"text":"Behavioural research groups"},{"text":"Human factors laboratories"},{"text":"University research centres"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other industries"},{"type":"p","text":"UX research also exists in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Banking"},{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"E-commerce"},{"text":"FinTech"},{"text":"Consumer products"},{"text":"Automotive"},{"text":"Telecommunications"}]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certificates are secondary to actual research experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritise learning in:"},{"type":"h","text":"UX"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX research"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"User-centred design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Survey methodology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analytics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Python/R"},{"text":"Product analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design collaboration"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop working familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Wireframes"},{"text":"User flows"},{"text":"Prototyping"}]},{"type":"p","text":"You do not need to become a full UI designer to work as a UX researcher."}]},{"heading":"Jobs You Can Be Hired For","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Direct-entry roles"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate can target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX Research Assistant"},{"text":"UX Research Intern"},{"text":"User Research Assistant"},{"text":"Junior UX Researcher"},{"text":"Research Assistant – UX"},{"text":"Human Factors Research Assistant"},{"text":"Design Research Assistant"},{"text":"Product Research Assistant"},{"text":"Customer Insights Analyst"},{"text":"User Insights Analyst"},{"text":"Research Analyst"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important distinction"},{"type":"p","text":"UX Research Assistant is an appropriate entry-level target."},{"type":"p","text":"The degree alone does not make someone a UX researcher. Employers will want evidence that the candidate can actually:"},{"type":"flow","items":["plan","conduct","analyse","communicate user research"]}]},{"heading":"Employer-Ready Portfolio","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A UX research portfolio is one of the most important hiring assets."},{"type":"p","text":"Create 3–5 detailed case studies."},{"type":"p","text":"Each case study should show:"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Problem"},{"type":"p","text":"What were you trying to understand?"},{"type":"h","text":"2. Research question"},{"type":"p","text":"What specifically did you investigate?"},{"type":"h","text":"3. Method"},{"type":"p","text":"Why did you choose:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview?"},{"text":"Survey?"},{"text":"Usability test?"},{"text":"Experiment?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Participants"},{"type":"p","text":"Who participated and why?"},{"type":"h","text":"5. Findings"},{"type":"p","text":"What did the evidence show?"},{"type":"h","text":"6. Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Show:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Themes"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Behavioural patterns"},{"text":"Statistical results"}]},{"type":"h","text":"7. Insights"},{"type":"p","text":"What does the evidence mean?"},{"type":"h","text":"8. Recommendations"},{"type":"p","text":"What should the product team change?"},{"type":"p","text":"This is much stronger than a portfolio containing only screenshots of interfaces."}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"1. Product UX Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital products"},{"text":"Mobile apps"},{"text":"SaaS"},{"text":"User behaviour"},{"text":"Product decisions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Human Factors"},{"type":"p","text":"Particularly relevant to neuroscience."},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human performance"},{"text":"Cognitive load"},{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Human-machine interaction"},{"text":"Error prevention"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential industries:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Aviation"},{"text":"Automotive"},{"text":"Defence"},{"text":"Industrial systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Behavioural Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Behaviour change"},{"text":"Cognitive biases"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Healthcare UX"},{"type":"p","text":"Use neuroscience/biomedical knowledge in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare applications"},{"text":"Clinical software"},{"text":"Digital health"},{"text":"Medical devices"},{"text":"Patient portals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This can be a particularly strong interdisciplinary niche."},{"type":"h","text":"5. AI / Human-AI Interaction"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trust in AI"},{"text":"Explainability"},{"text":"Human-AI collaboration"},{"text":"AI usability"},{"text":"User expectations"},{"text":"Automation bias"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is likely to become increasingly important."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Options in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A PG is not mandatory for UX Research Assistant roles, but it can be valuable for specialised research careers."},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant programmes"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Cognitive Science"},{"text":"M.Sc Neuroscience"},{"text":"M.Sc Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"M.Des Interaction Design"},{"text":"M.Des User Experience Design"},{"text":"M.Sc Human Factors"},{"text":"M.Sc Behavioural Science"},{"text":"MA Psychology"},{"text":"M.Sc Psychology"},{"text":"M.Sc Data Science / Analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For design-focused programmes, check portfolio and entrance requirements carefully."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"USA"},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant fields:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"User Experience Research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"UK"},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant fields:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Interaction Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Canada"},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HCI"},{"text":"Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"UX Research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Australia"},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HCI"},{"text":"Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Interaction Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Europe"},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Cognitive Systems"},{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Interaction Design"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Neuroscience / Cognitive Science","UX Research Intern / Research Assistant","Junior UX Researcher","UX Researcher","Senior UX Researcher","Lead UX Researcher","UX Research Manager","Head of UX Research / Research Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["UX Research","Human Factors / Behavioural Science","Senior Research Specialist","Behavioural Science / Human Factors Lead"]}]},{"heading":"PhD & Research Directions","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students interested in advanced research can pursue:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive neuroscience"},{"text":"Human-computer interaction"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Behavioural science"},{"text":"Decision science"},{"text":"Computational cognitive science"},{"text":"Human-AI interaction"},{"text":"Neuroergonomics"},{"text":"Cognitive load"},{"text":"Attention and perception"},{"text":"User behaviour modelling"},{"text":"Brain-computer interaction"}]}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Future Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"UX research is likely to become increasingly focused on human behaviour in AI-mediated environments."},{"type":"h","text":"Human-AI interaction"},{"type":"p","text":"Researchers will study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Why users trust AI"},{"text":"When users distrust AI"},{"text":"Automation bias"},{"text":"Human oversight"},{"text":"Explainability"},{"text":"AI decision-making"},{"text":"AI-assisted workflows"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neuroadaptive interfaces"},{"type":"p","text":"Advances in sensors may allow systems to respond to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Cognitive workload"},{"text":"Stress indicators"},{"text":"User behaviour"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This creates opportunities at the intersection of:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Neuroscience","UX","AI","Human Factors"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"AI-assisted UX research"},{"type":"p","text":"AI will increasingly assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview transcription"},{"text":"Qualitative coding"},{"text":"Theme detection"},{"text":"Survey analysis"},{"text":"Research synthesis"},{"text":"Behavioural pattern discovery"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Researchers will still need to validate findings because automated analysis can introduce errors, bias, or misleading interpretations."},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-AI Interaction Researcher"},{"text":"Behavioural UX Researcher"},{"text":"Cognitive UX Specialist"},{"text":"Human Factors Researcher"},{"text":"AI UX Researcher"},{"text":"Neuroergonomics Researcher"},{"text":"Behavioural Data Scientist"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Cognitive foundation"},{"type":"flow","items":["Neuroscience","Cognitive Psychology","Behavioural Science"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Qualitative Research","Quantitative Research","Experimental Design","Research Ethics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"UX"},{"type":"flow","items":["User Interviews","Usability Testing","Survey Design","User Journeys","Human-Computer Interaction"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Analytics"},{"type":"flow","items":["Statistics","Excel","SQL","Python/R","Product Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Communication"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Writing","Storytelling","Presentation","Stakeholder Communication"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Design collaboration"},{"type":"flow","items":["Figma","Wireframing","Prototyping","Information Architecture"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Future"},{"type":"flow","items":["Human-AI Interaction","Behavioural Analytics","AI-Assisted Research"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Ideal Graduate Profile","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, an ideal UX Research Assistant candidate should be able to:"},{"type":"p","text":"Design and execute a small-scale UX research study, recruit and interview appropriate participants, conduct usability testing, analyse qualitative and quantitative evidence, identify behavioural and cognitive patterns, communicate research insights clearly, and translate those insights into practical product recommendations."},{"type":"h","text":"Best practical pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Neuroscience / Cognitive Science","Cognitive Psychology + Statistics","Research Methodology","UX Research","User Interviews & Usability Testing","Qualitative/Quantitative Analysis","UX Research Portfolio","UX Research Internship","UX Research Assistant","UX Researcher","Senior UX Researcher / Human Factors Specialist","Research Leadership"]}]}]}